[00:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Welcome to this introduction of the anti-gravity A1 vision goggles and grip controller. The vision goggles feature two ports at the bottom, a power port and a USB C'

[00:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'port. Connect the vision goggles battery to the vision goggles using the battery cable. Thread the vision goggles battery cable through the headband as shown.'

[00:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Press and hold the power button on the battery for approximately 2 seconds to power on the vision goggles. The adjustment knob controls lens'

[00:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'distance and diopter settings. If your vision falls between 500 to 800 diopters, you can unscrew the original frame counterclockwise and remove it.'

[00:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Replace it with the included Myopia correction lenses from the package. Install the lens assembly onto the barrel at the angle shown in the video. Screw the frame clockwise with moderate'

[01:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'force until you hear a click. The left side of the vision goggles features the home button. Double click to enable see-through, allowing you to observe your surroundings without removing the'

[01:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'goggles. A long press pairs the drone with the grip controller. The right side houses the volume buttons to adjust the audio level. Above the nose bridge are the micro SD card slot and proximity sensor.'

[01:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'The headband is pre-installed before you\'ve even unboxed your drone. Adjust the Velcro strap position according to your head circumference and for comfort.'

[01:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'The front right side features the outer display, enabling sharing of the vision goggles view with others. The USBC port at the bottom of the grip controller is for charging. During charging, the'

[01:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'battery indicator light flashes in a cycle. When all indicator lights remain steadily lit, the battery is full charged. Front controls include unlock slider used for unlocking and drone'

[02:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'takeoff landing. Brake/RTH button. Long press initiates auto return to home. Short press for brakes during flight or cancels a return command. 360'

[02:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'view dial. Rotate left right to control horizontal rotation. Short press centers the drone\'s view. Quickly aligns the navigation point. plus a photo button'

[02:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and video button. On the right side of the grip controller, you\'ll find power button. Short press displays current battery level. Short press followed by a long press'

[02:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'approx 2 seconds powers the grip controller on or off. Menu button. Press to bring up the menu in the vision goggles. You can also press and hold the menu'

[03:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'button to bring up the quick menu. Navigate to the desired function area. Then release the button to execute the operation. And on the left side of the grip controller, flight mode switch cycles'

[03:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'through sport, normal, and cinematic modes. Customizable C1, C2 buttons. At the front, you have the accelerator trigger. When the drone is not in flight or is'

[03:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'hovering, press the menu button on the grip controller to activate the virtual laser pointer for menu navigation. Move the grip controller up, down, left, or right to control the virtual laser'

[03:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'pointer\'s position within the vision goggles display. If the pointer moves off screen, press the 360 view dial to quickly center it again. Position the virtual laser pointer over'

[03:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a menu option and press the accelerator trigger. The circle at the pointer\'s tip will turn orange and shrink, indicating a click that opens the corresponding menu. Hold the accelerator trigger while'

[04:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'rotating your wrist up, down, left, or right to scroll through menu pages. Adjust brightness, volume, and other settings. In certain specialized flight interfaces, the virtual laser pointer'

[04:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'may also activate. Follow onscreen prompts to use it for specific operations. Thanks for watching.'
